Enhancement: Make pack uploads resilient and clean up orphaned packs

Backing up a repository with high write concurrency could leave duplicate
or orphaned pack files in the backend when an upload failed after the data
was already stored, and retrying could upload the same pack twice. Restic
now retries failed pack uploads with an exponential backoff, skips a pack
that is already present in the backend, and tracks open pack handles so
that each pack is uploaded at most once. Packs left behind by an
interrupted backup are detected and removed at the start of the next
backup. Underfilled packs are flushed on shutdown and their temporary
files are released on error paths.
